# data
{% if kind == 'data-pipeline' %}
`raw/` holds each source exactly as downloaded, beside a `<file>.fetch.json` record:
the URL, retrieval time, SHA-256 and vintage. `processed/` holds what `just build`
derives from it, plus `datapackage.json`, a Frictionless Data Package that lists
each output with its columns, checksum, source URL and licence. Both are gitignored. `just pipeline` rebuilds them from
`sources.toml`, so the repository never redistributes source data. Never edit a
raw file in place: `just build` and `just validate` both reject one whose checksum
no longer matches its fetch record.

`fetches.jsonl` is committed. `just fetch` appends a source's fetch record to it each
time it brings bytes that source has not had before, so the file is the history of
every version the pipeline has seen. Commit it after a fetch that changes it.
{%- else %}
Put inputs in `raw/` and derived files in `processed/`; create them as you need them.
`raw/` is read-only input: never edit it in place. The notebooks rebuild `processed/`
from `raw/`, so you can delete it.

Record the provenance of anything in `raw/` here. Add these directories to
`.gitignore` if the inputs are large or private.
{%- endif %}
